                <pb facs="0619" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/799a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-17T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>124. Department’s 354, October 1, 4 p.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d479-f1"/> What is
                    present status of proposed surtax? It is intimated to the Department that
                    objection of Japan only is preventing collection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
